  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-10-25T16:24:31.714Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "It would be lovely if world creators could force disable certain avatar features like collider flight / lights / etc. via the SDK to create more tailored experiences.\n\nThis could be implemented into the SDK by using the already preexisting Tagging system used for worlds.  A tag like \"avatar_disallow_collider_flight\" will disallow collider components on avatars either by forcing them off or by removing them on load (I know this would break things like avatar chairs so a more in-depth approach would be needed like changing collider layers or something).\n\nThis would be great for certain game worlds as it'll prevent cheating via using flight colliders.  Another example would be disabling someone's avatar lights in a horror world so the horror isn't lost on them as they walk through a unlit world.",
